{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context and confirmed root cause\n\nThe accepted benchmark on closed ticket left-changeful-mamba deliberately requires 3,000 tickets, 6,000 events, exactly 24 batched commits, and >=10x commit-count reduction. It is the integration-tier long pole at 93-108s on current macOS jobs. N, event count, commit/crash safety, platform cells, and coverage are locked.\n\nA full N=3000 cProfile on current origin/main confirmed two dynamic bulk-path defects:\n- rebar._commands._seam.append_event calls author(), which executes git config user.name once per envelope. The benchmark made 6,000 calls; _git_config consumed 47.79s cumulative and subprocess.run 59.54s.\n- event_append.batch_stage_and_commit prepares a chunk by calling staging.stage_event for every not-yet-published CREATE. stage_event calls sweep_stale_staging for each new ticket, so the benchmark made 3,000 sweeps and 375,876 staging-owner checks, consuming 15.94s. Within a batch, the same staging root is rescanned while earlier prepared items remain unpublished.\n\nControlled identical-harness A/B, preserving 3,000 creates, 3,000 comments, and 29 total commits (5 init + the locked 24 import delta):\n- current collaborators with counting wrappers: 77.231s, 6,001 git-config reads, 3,000 sweeps;\n- only git-config and sweep replaced by side-effect-free logical collaborators: 16.404s, same state and commits.\nThat 60.8s delta discriminates these mechanisms from event serialization/commit count as the dominant avoidable cost.\n\n## OSS comparison and prior decisions\n\nGit's maintained fast-import backend reads one stream and writes repository objects/refs in bulk (git/git@745601a, Documentation/git-fast-import.adoc#L14-L29). The relevant consensus is amortizing repeat setup/scans inside a bulk boundary, not replacing rebar's event validation or crash-safe commits with git fast-import.\n\nTracker cross-check: left-changeful-mamba locks N=3000, 6,000 events, 24 commits, >=10x reduction, rollback, and crash-resume. coercive-paediatric-bug rejects extra workers/shards that increase runner-minutes. No ticket rejects batch-scoped identity lookup or one stale-staging sweep per batch; interactive per-write behavior remains unchanged.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. In src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py add an explicit contextvar-scoped author cache. Outside that context author() retains the existing per-call git-config read. The cache is keyed by fallback so git-config-less Unknown/unknown parity remains. It is nestable and reset in finally.\n2. In src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py enter that author-cache context for the whole import composition. Every imported envelope therefore uses the author value observed once at import start; no cache survives the call, thread/task, or pytest session. Event bytes and attribution fields are otherwise unchanged.\n3. In src/rebar/_store/staging.py let stage_event skip its per-item stale sweep only when its caller has already performed the sweep. The default remains sweep-enabled for every direct/single-event caller.\n4. In src/rebar/_store/event_append.py materialize each bounded chunk, preserve the empty-batch no-op, perform one stale-staging sweep when the batch contains any ticket whose directory does not yet exist, then prepare all items with per-item sweeping disabled. Validation, atomic staging/publish, rollback, lock, and commit behavior remain unchanged.\n5. Strengthen the existing N=3000 integration benchmark with deterministic counters: one user.name lookup for the import and one stale sweep per CREATE chunk (ceil(3000/256)=12), never wall-clock thresholds. Add focused unit coverage that empty batches do not sweep, existing-ticket-only batches do not introduce a new sweep, new-ticket batches sweep once, direct stage_event still sweeps, fallback-sensitive author caching is scoped, and interactive writes remain uncached.\n6. RED first on the current mechanisms, hold the oracle out from the fixer, then GREEN. Re-seed each defect independently (remove author cache; restore per-item sweep) and prove the corresponding assertion returns RED. Refactoring-only renames must remain green.\n7. Re-run the identical N=3000 harness/profile on the same host and report wall/call-count deltas. Run import batching/idempotency/crash-resume/rollback, atomic ticket-dir/store tests, lint, typecheck, and the full pytest selection.\n\n## Test contract card\n\nauthoritative_contract: left-changeful-mamba plus tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py require N=3000, 6,000 events, exactly 24 crash-safe commits, >=10x reduction, complete created/comment counts, rollback and resume; this ticket requires eliminating redundant bulk setup without changing those contracts.\ntrigger_preconditions: a fresh git-backed store importing 3,000 synthetic CREATE+comment records through public rebar.import_tickets.\nproduction_path: rebar.import_tickets -> import_ndjson.import_tickets -> _seam.append_event/finalize_event -> event_append.batch_stage_and_commit -> staging.stage_event.\ntest_tier: real temporary-git integration for the locked import contract plus focused unit tests for cache/sweep lifecycle.\nobservable_postcondition: identical logical state and 24 import commits; exactly one user.name lookup per import; exactly 12 stale sweeps for the 12 CREATE chunks; single/direct writes retain their existing lookup/sweep behavior.\nnegative_control: interactive writes remain one commit and one live author lookup per event; existing-ticket-only/empty batches do not gain stale-sweep work.\ncollateral_invariants: same event bytes/author fallback semantics, clean index, no lost/duplicate events, same warnings and provenance.\nrecovery: injected later-chunk commit failure resumes to all tickets exactly once.\nci_gate: integration pytest job and full Gerrit Verified gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] N=3000, 6,000 events, created/comment counts, exactly 24 commits, and >=10x assertions remain unchanged and pass.\n- [ ] The integration oracle records exactly one git config user.name lookup for the import and exactly 12 stale-staging sweeps for CREATE chunks; both are deterministic, non-wall-clock assertions.\n- [ ] Interactive/direct writes retain live author lookup and stale-sweep behavior; cache/context and batch optimizations cannot leak across calls, threads/tasks, or sessions.\n- [ ] Each defect-seeded mutation independently returns the held-out oracle to RED; the restored change is GREEN.\n- [ ] Identical-host before/after evidence reports importer time and profiler call counts; timing is evidence, never a gate threshold.\n- [ ] Import idempotency, crash-resume, rollback, per-event equivalence, atomic ticket-directory, clean-index, lint, typecheck, full pytest, LLM-Review, and Verified are green.\n- [ ] No dependency, durability/public behavior, platform, Python-matrix, test, mutation, or coverage assurance is removed."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786639111882611001,"uuid":"987cfffc-4054-4c0c-a85e-709b09bf1a68"}